{"duration_api_ms":8209,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5ddbec8b-0dd8-4c2d-8f20-cf4c46375f33","total_cost_usd":0.0011415000000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1711,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1296},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1711,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1267,"outputTokens":1740,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":724,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0011415000000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1296,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":724,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Cross-subsidization**\n- **Mutual fund → ETF:** Mutual fund cash redemptions force portfolio sales, generating trading costs and realized gains that can be spread across all holders, including ETF shareholders.\n- **ETF → mutual fund:** Cash-settled ETF creations and redemptions require trades that burden the shared portfolio, so mutual fund holders can bear those costs. In-kind ETF redemptions can purge low-basis lots, which may benefit everyone.\n\n**Monitoring categories**\n- **Transaction costs:** Attribute spreads, market impact, and commissions to the originating class.\n- **Cash:** Track flow-driven cash balances and allocate cash drag by class.\n- **Gains:** Track realized gains by source (cash vs. in-kind) and by lot selection.\n\n**Conceptual example (illustrative):** A $10M mutual fund redemption that forces a $10M sale of appreciated holdings can realize gains shared across all classes.\n\n**Representative order-specific framework (illustrative):** Tag each order with its class of origin, settlement type (cash or in-kind), and cost components, then allocate accordingly. Thresholds and allocation methods should follow the board-approved policy, not a universal standard.","ttft_ms":6298,"type":"result","duration_ms":7568,"uuid":"dfeb2a77-bfe8-4afc-910c-2a76cf8dd6b8","ttft_stream_ms":407,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":407,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
